{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44129726",
      "title": "Validating Input with Form Validation Directives",
      "lectureOrder": 246,
      "videoOrder": 234,
      "sourceHash": "48496329113ec76b8383f5c8f73dc284a7d87e282d20ed06ce8484e2d1c79ece",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 4.5,
          "en": "So, how can we handle form validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.5,
          "end": 6.75,
          "en": "with help of Angular?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.75,
          "end": 9.96,
          "en": "Well, when using this template-driven approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.96,
          "end": 14.52,
          "en": "so when using ng model to register controls, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.52,
          "end": 18.63,
          "en": "you can add special validation directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.63,
          "end": 21.99,
          "en": "or attributes to your input elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.99,
          "end": 25.89,
          "en": "And some of these attributes are standard attributes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.89,
          "end": 29.58,
          "en": "you could add to vanilla HTML elements as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.58,
          "end": 32.493,
          "en": "Like, for example, the required attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.36,
          "end": 35.46,
          "en": "I'll actually add it after ng model here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.46,
          "end": 37.41,
          "en": "but the position doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.41,
          "end": 40.62,
          "en": "You could add that to a standard HTML element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.62,
          "end": 43.35,
          "en": "that's not managed by Angular as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.35,
          "end": 48.24,
          "en": "and you would get some browser built-in validation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.24,
          "end": 50.94,
          "en": "But when using it on an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.94,
          "end": 54.06,
          "en": "that is registered with ng model,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.06,
          "end": 55.92,
          "en": "Angular will actually take over",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.92,
          "end": 59.43,
          "en": "and disable the browser built in validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.43,
          "end": 63.003,
          "en": "and instead validate it itself internally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.99,
          "end": 68.28,
          "en": "Because required is essentially registered as a directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.28,
          "end": 70.38,
          "en": "with Angular, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.38,
          "end": 74.01,
          "en": "and when used on an element that also uses ng model,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.01,
          "end": 76.59,
          "en": "Angular under the hood will check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.59,
          "end": 80.97,
          "en": "whether a value has been entered into this input field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.97,
          "end": 83.7,
          "en": "Because required simply tells Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.7,
          "end": 86.4,
          "en": "that this input field must not be empty.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.4,
          "end": 88.59,
          "en": "So Angular will check for that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.59,
          "end": 91.26,
          "en": "and will tell you if that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.26,
          "end": 95.91,
          "en": "And I'll show you how it tells you in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.91,
          "end": 99.18299999999999,
          "en": "We can also add required here on the password input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.35,
          "end": 103.32,
          "en": "Now in addition, this input should also be an email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.32,
          "end": 104.31,
          "en": "and that's why we can add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.31,
          "end": 107.75999999999999,
          "en": "the special email directive to this input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.75999999999999,
          "end": 110.75999999999999,
          "en": "or email attribute if you wanna call it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.75999999999999,
          "end": 114.18,
          "en": "But that's also registered as a directive by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.18,
          "end": 115.14,
          "en": "in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.14,
          "end": 118.22999999999999,
          "en": "And it will, in the end, check whether a valid email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.22999999999999,
          "end": 120.12,
          "en": "has been entered here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.12,
          "end": 121.65,
          "en": "For the password input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.65,
          "end": 125.64,
          "en": "I wanna make sure that it's at least six characters long",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.64,
          "end": 129.18,
          "en": "and we can do that by adding the minlength attribute here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.18,
          "end": 130.833,
          "en": "and setting this to six.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.97,
          "end": 135.453,
          "en": "And that's then also registered by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.82999999999998,
          "end": 140.52,
          "en": "So, these are some of the most common directives you can add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.52,
          "end": 142.41,
          "en": "to add validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.41,
          "end": 146.91,
          "en": "or to enforce validation with help of Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.91,
          "end": 149.76,
          "en": "And there also would be others like max",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.76,
          "end": 154.41,
          "en": "if you wanted to allow a maximum number in an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.41,
          "end": 156.18,
          "en": "or min if you want to ensure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.18,
          "end": 160.05,
          "en": "that no number lower than this min number can be entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.05,
          "end": 163.56,
          "en": "in case you have some kind of numeric input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.56,
          "end": 165.6,
          "en": "There also is max length",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 165.6,
          "end": 167.733,
          "en": "if you care about the max length,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.87,
          "end": 170.88,
          "en": "and pattern if you want to register",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 170.88,
          "end": 173.1,
          "en": "your own regular expression pattern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 173.1,
          "end": 174.963,
          "en": "that should be used for validation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.92000000000002,
          "end": 177.27,
          "en": "Now here I only want to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.27,
          "end": 181.05,
          "en": "these validation directives here though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 181.05,
          "end": 184.11,
          "en": "and if I add them and save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.11,
          "end": 188.11,
          "en": "you'll notice that I can still submit an empty form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.03,
          "end": 193.59,
          "en": "because that's really important to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.59,
          "end": 196.82999999999998,
          "en": "Adding these validation attributes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.82999999999998,
          "end": 199.02,
          "en": "these validation directives here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.02,
          "end": 204.02,
          "en": "does not tell Angular that it should prevent form submission",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204.6,
          "end": 206.133,
          "en": "or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 207.36,
          "end": 212.36,
          "en": "Instead it will just change some internally managed values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 213.27,
          "end": 215.88,
          "en": "and therefore back in the login component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 215.88,
          "end": 220.88,
          "en": "I will console log this form object, which we get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.6,
          "end": 227.6,
          "en": "which is managed by Angular to see what changed there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.24,
          "end": 231.03,
          "en": "Because now if I submitted that empty form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 231.03,
          "end": 233.55,
          "en": "I got this form group object here again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.55,
          "end": 234.93,
          "en": "And if we expand that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.93,
          "end": 238.14,
          "en": "we can now see that in there the status,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 238.14,
          "end": 239.643,
          "en": "for example, is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 242.552,
          "end": 245.94,
          "en": "And if I go to the controls, I see that, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 245.94,
          "end": 250.71,
          "en": "for the email control, the status is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 250.71,
          "end": 254.61,
          "en": "And I can see that there I got an errors key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 254.61,
          "end": 257.67,
          "en": "which now holds an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 257.67,
          "end": 260.13,
          "en": "where required is set to true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 260.13,
          "end": 263.82,
          "en": "which in the end tells me that it's the required validator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 263.82,
          "end": 265.32,
          "en": "that failed here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 265.32,
          "end": 267.003,
          "en": "So that was not met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.9,
          "end": 269.67,
          "en": "If I, for example, enter something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 269.67,
          "end": 273.39,
          "en": "that's not an email address and I submit this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 273.39,
          "end": 278.19,
          "en": "I see that, still, the overall form status is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 278.19,
          "end": 283.19,
          "en": "But now for the email control errors, is email true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 283.29,
          "end": 286.74,
          "en": "Because now the required validator was met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 286.74,
          "end": 289.47,
          "en": "It's not an empty input field after all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.47,
          "end": 291.42,
          "en": "but it's not an email address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 291.42,
          "end": 294.93,
          "en": "So the email validator basically told Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 294.93,
          "end": 298.74,
          "en": "that this email control is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 298.74,
          "end": 301.02,
          "en": "So this is what changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 301.02,
          "end": 306.02,
          "en": "if we add those validation attributes and directives here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 306.12,
          "end": 309.12,
          "en": "And we can therefore use this information, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 309.12,
          "end": 311.22,
          "en": "when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 311.22,
          "end": 312.78,
          "en": "Here, right at the start,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 312.78,
          "end": 317.78,
          "en": "I can check a form data form valid if that is true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 320.49,
          "end": 325.49,
          "en": "because the overall form does have a valid property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 327.42,
          "end": 330.423,
          "en": "which is false here, if it is invalid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 332.4,
          "end": 334.8,
          "en": "So I can check if this overall form is valid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 334.8,
          "end": 338.52,
          "en": "or, to be precise, if it's not valid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 338.52,
          "end": 341.07,
          "en": "Or alternatively, there actually also is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 341.07,
          "end": 344.22,
          "en": "an invalid property, which I can simply check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 344.22,
          "end": 346.65,
          "en": "And if this form is invalid, then I can,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 346.65,
          "end": 348.96,
          "en": "for example, just return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 348.96,
          "end": 350.7,
          "en": "to make sure that none of this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 350.7,
          "end": 354.65999999999997,
          "en": "will execute if an invalid form has been submitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 354.65999999999997,
          "end": 357.51,
          "en": "which will essentially make sure that nothing happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 357.51,
          "end": 360.78,
          "en": "if an invalid form was submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 360.78,
          "end": 363.66,
          "en": "That's one thing we might want to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 363.66,
          "end": 367.383,
          "en": "But we can also do more than just that.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
